 "<1/>Let midnight indigo carry the layout; colour arrives as an event.": "",
 "<1/>One gold action per view. If two things are gold, neither is primary.": "",
 "<1/>Use sky for what informs — links, data, guides — and gold for what converts.": "",
 "<1/>Set text on gold in midnight indigo, always.": "",
 "<1/>Bring in cool white for long reading and a change of pace.": "",
 "<1/>Don’t use pure black or pure white. Our dark is indigo; our white is cool.": "",
 "<1/>Don’t give gold and sky equal weight — sky is always the quieter of the two.": "",
 "<1/>Don’t set gold or sky text on white; both fail contrast.": "",
 "<1/>Don’t turn gold into a gradient, a glow or a metallic effect.": "",
 "<1/>Don’t use orange as a brand colour — it is reserved for warnings.": "",
